Author: vvondruska <vondruska.vaclav@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 13 14:04:52 2026 +0200

    test(transport): make failed setup name itself (#18)

    Both transport test files took an id out of a creation response without
    checking the response. When that request did not return a chat, the id
    was undefined, the next request went to a path containing the word
    undefined, and the failure surfaced somewhere else entirely: once as a
    missing workspace two assertions later.

    In createApp.test.ts it was worse than confusing. The test that proves
    two apps do not share a store expects a 404, so a creation that failed
    satisfied it, and the test passed for the wrong reason.

    Both now throw, naming the status and body they actually got. Throwing
    rather than asserting keeps one expect per test, which the lint rule
    requires.


