commit fc0e424dc5687764192efc1392555ecb95839424
Author: vvondruska <vaclav@re-cinq.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 11 22:07:16 2026 +0200

    fix(transport): record the chat requests it refuses

    The routes answered 401 and wrote nothing. grep -c "log\." over
    chats.ts returned 0: the file did not import the logger at all, so an
    access-control decision left no trace anywhere. An operator could not
    tell a misconfigured auth middleware from an absent one, or a probe from
    a typo, and nothing downstream could alert on either.

    Both refusal paths now go through one `deny` helper emitting a single
    warn on category `http`. The two call sites pass a fixed string - "no
    auth middleware is configured" or "the configured middleware attached no
    usable user id" - so the line says which of the two states the router is
    in, which is the thing an operator needs and the thing the status code
    cannot carry.

    Nothing request-derived is logged. `reason` is chosen at the call site,
    never built from the request, so a refusal cannot become the second place
    a chat id or a query string comes to rest. A test asserts that by
    requesting a distinctive id and checking it appears nowhere in the
    emitted lines.

    Four tests, using the setLogger export added earlier in this branch
    rather than spying on console: exactly one warn per refusal on each path,
    nothing request-derived in the data, and silence on an authorised
    request - so the line means a refusal rather than traffic.

    Coverage floor moves up with the measurement: 78.71 lines.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LwoztdBKudtfu3JJkfamWx

