commit 5beaed9d8e51bc3d9f6999c35cf28317ab70ce70
Author: vvondruska <vaclav@re-cinq.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 11 16:03:03 2026 +0200

    fix(transport): deny the chat routes when no auth is configured

    T012. createChatRoutes took an optional authMiddleware and fell back to a
    pass-through, so a deployment that configured none served every caller as
    one shared anonymous user - anyone holding a chat id could read it and
    post to it.

    The fallback is now a 401. It sits where the pass-through did, ahead of
    the route handler, so the denial precedes the chat lookup and an
    unauthenticated caller cannot use 404-versus-401 to probe which ids
    exist. Signatures are unchanged: the middleware stays optional, and
    configuring one is unaffected.

    Middleware that runs but attaches no user is a separate case and still
    passes through. That is T013's, and the spec now separates the two rather
    than describing them as one.

    All four new tests fail against the old fallback and pass against this
    one; the eleven existing tests are unmoved either way, which is the
    evidence that nothing but the unconfigured path changed.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CyFimiuBEQXWWBktCx6gHE

